<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Li Hongzhang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Li Hongzhang was a leading Chinese statesman and general of the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>. He played a major role in suppressing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion">Taiping Rebellion</a> and promoted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/self-strengthening-movement">Self-Strengthening Movement</a>, building arsenals, industries and a modern navy. He negotiated several treaties after Qing defeats, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-shimonoseki">Treaty of Shimonoseki</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 1895.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/li-hongzhang.jpg" alt="Li Hongzhang" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Russell &amp;amp; Sons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Li_Hung_Chang_in_1896(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
